 CheckTempFolder(name ps);⎕TRAP
⍝ Called by Tester2 after every single test, but only when `T.exec_after_each_test` names
⍝ this function; see `Initial`, where the assignment sits commented out.
⍝ It suspends rather than reports, hence ⎕TRAP←0 'S': the test that caused the problem is
⍝ then still on the stack, and `name` says which one it was.
⍝ What's checked:
⍝ A "SomeGroup" package in the Registry of the test server. Only `Test_UC_002` and
⍝ `Test_UC_007` ever publish one, and both delete it again in their ∆TidyUp. One that
⍝ survives a test means ∆TidyUp did not get that far, and whichever of the two runs next
⍝ is then told that its first publish has already been published - which neither expects.
⍝ `Test_UC_007` has no automated answer for the question that follows, so it waits for one.
 ⎕TRAP←0 'S'
 :If 0<⎕NC'∆TEMP_SERVER_FOLDER'                    ⍝ Undefined until `Initial` has run
     {⍵:.}0<≢⊃F.Dir ∆TEMP_SERVER_FOLDER,'SomeGroup-*'
 :EndIf
⍝Done
